# Build-context exclusions for EVERY image built from the monorepo context
# (property-pub, bizchat, and the `monorepo` additional_context of 4prop-web).
#
# SCOPE THIS NARROWLY. One file governs several images, so anything excluded here
# is invisible to all of them — an over-broad rule fails at build time in an image
# you were not thinking about.

# ── property-pub: the UK postcodemap GeoJSON ────────────────────────────────
# ~12MB of static polygons, PUBLISHED TO THE SHARED UPLOADS VOLUME instead of baked
# in (`npm run deploy:postcodemap`). Excluded because it shared a Docker layer with
# the application code, which changes on every deploy — so 12MB of unchanged
# geometry was rebuilt and re-pushed to the registry each time.
#
# Read at runtime via getPostcodemapDir() → UPLOADS_PATH; nothing imports it at
# build time. PUBLISH BEFORE DEPLOYING an image without it: the static route is
# `fallthrough: false`, so a missing directory 404s rather than serving HTML.
apps/backend/property-pub/code/src/data/postcodemap

# ── never useful in any image ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# node_modules is reinstalled inside the image (`npm install` against the copied
# package.json files), so shipping the host's 876MB copy would be both slow and
# wrong — it carries the host platform's native binaries (sharp's darwin build
# instead of the linuxmusl one).
**/node_modules
**/.git
